(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "cloud-itonami-isic-0240 support-services-to-forestry forestry-support-service operations coordination actor implementation" "fresh scaffold closing the kotoba-lang/industry placeholder gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0240 gap")), (:adr/topic "cloud-itonami-isic-0240-forestry-support-services-coverage"), (:adr/related (vector "cloud-itonami-isic-0161")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2613100000-cloud-itonami-isic-0240-forestry-support-services-coverage"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-16"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2613100000: cloud-itonami-isic-0240 (Support services to forestry) forestry-support-service operations-coordination actor -- fresh scaffold, full implementation\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-16\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)\n**Related**: cloud-itonami-isic-0161 (Support activities for crop\nproduction -- the reference module shape this actor mirrors, independently\nre-read in full before use), the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry's\n`\"0240\"` catalog entry (previously `:spec` with a placeholder\n`gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0240` repo link that was never populated)\n\n## Context\n\n`kotoba-lang/industry`'s registry carried a `\"0240\"` entry at `:maturity\n:spec` pointing at `https://github.com/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0240` -- a\nplaceholder repo link with no actual implementation behind it (no source,\nno tests; confirmed 404 via `gh api` for both the placeholder and the real\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0240` before any work began). This is\npart of an ongoing careful, smaller-batch rollout (one ISIC class per\nagent, a capable model, mandatory verification) after a prior 18-agent\nhaiku batch produced a 61% defect rate on other ISIC classes; 138+\nconsecutive agents on this stricter protocol had all succeeded since. This\nADR covers ISIC 0240 only. Before any work began, the registry entry's\nidentity (`{:id \"0240\" :name \"Support services to forestry\"}`) was\nindependently verified against a fresh clone of `kotoba-lang/industry`,\nper this fleet's caution against ID/name mismatches (prior agents in this\nfleet had mislabeled other ISIC classes) -- confirmed correct, no\nmismatch. ISIC 0240 covers CONTRACT LOGGING-SUPPORT SERVICES: cruising\n(timber-resource survey), forest-fire-protection support, seed collection,\nand transport of logs within the forest -- distinct from actual timber\nharvesting (felling) itself, which sits in ISIC's timber-harvesting\ndivisions (022x).\n\n## Decision\n\nScaffold `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0240` as a forestry-SUPPORT-\nSERVICE OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor (not direct forestry-equipment\noperation authority, not a fire-suppression-tactics authority), mirroring\n`cloud-itonami-isic-0161`'s verified module shape\n(`facts`/`registry`/`store`/`governor`/`operation`/`phase`/`advisor`/\n`sim`, `deps.edn`/`blueprint.edn`/README/GOVERNANCE/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/\nCONTRIBUTING/SECURITY) with fresh, forestry-support-service-specific\ndomain logic under the `forestrysupport` namespace. ISIC 0240 covers\nCONTRACT logging-support work performed for OTHER forest operators on a\nfee/contract basis -- the operator never fells or owns the standing\ntimber being serviced, which is what distinguishes this actor from the\nactual timber-harvesting divisions (022x) themselves, which drives every\ndomain-specific check below:\n\n1. **`forestrysupport.facts`** -- service-type safety windows split\n   across survey/collection service types (timber cruising, seed\n   collection -- no field-equipment-operation safety window at all,\n   `nil` for operator-certification/equipment-inspection/wind-speed/\n   riparian-buffer/load-limit fields) and field-equipment-operation\n   service types (forest-fire-protection support patrol-and-fuelbreak-\n   maintenance, in-forest log transport -- each with a genuine\n   operator-certification requirement, an equipment-inspection interval,\n   and -- where physically applicable to that specific service -- a\n   maximum fieldwork wind speed, a minimum riparian buffer, and a\n   maximum haul-road load), plus jurisdiction evidence-checklist\n   requirements (JP 森林法・林野庁 / US State Forest Practices Act / CA\n   British Columbia FRPA). Not every field-equipment-operation service\n   type carries every physical-constraint field -- in-forest log-haul\n   has no fieldwork wind-speed ceiling of its own (haul-road travel is\n   not wind-sensitive the way canopy-adjacent chainsaw fuel-break work\n   is) and fire-protection-support patrol/fuel-break work carries no\n   haul-road load limit (it hauls no logs) -- the Governor's\n   corresponding check is skipped entirely, never fabricated, when a\n   given service type's field is nil.\n2. **`forestrysupport.registry`** -- pure, host-clock-free validation\n   predicates the Governor uses to independently verify physical/\n   regulatory constraints: operator-certification expiry,\n   equipment-inspection overdue (per-type interval, not a single\n   hardcoded window -- fire-protection-support's 30-day interval is\n   stricter than log-transport's 60-day interval, a genuine domain\n   difference caught while writing the tests), wind-speed exceeded,\n   riparian-buffer violated, and load-limit exceeded.\n3. **`forestrysupport.store`** -- plain-data store (`{:service-orders\n   {...} :facts [...]}`) with service-order lookup/registration/logged/\n   scheduled flags and an append-only audit ledger.\n4. **`forestrysupport.governor`** -- 13 independently-verified\n   hard-violation checks plus a closed operation allowlist as a hard,\n   permanent block per the domain design: the advisor may only ever\n   propose `:log-service-record`, `:schedule-field-operation`,\n   `:flag-forest-health-concern`, `:order-supplies` (all `:effect\n   :propose`); anything else -- most importantly direct\n   chainsaw/skidder/patrol-vehicle control -- is refused unconditionally\n   (`:op-not-allowed`), never a soft escalation. A dedicated\n   `:forestry-equipment-or-fire-tactic-decision-blocked` check adds\n   defense-in-depth against a proposal that covertly requests direct\n   forestry-equipment control or a final fire-suppression-tactic\n   decision via a marker nested inside an otherwise-allowed op's\n   `:value` -- evaluated unconditionally against every op, a permanent\n   block never overridable by human approval, matching this fleet's\n   established pattern of structural (not merely documented) scope\n   boundaries. The `:service-order-not-registered` invariant is applied\n   across ALL FOUR allowed ops, per this actor's explicit domain-design\n   requirement that a service-order/client-forest-operator record be\n   independently verified/registered before any action at all.\n   `:flag-forest-health-concern` always escalates to a human regardless\n   of confidence, as does `:log-service-record` (the one real actuation\n   event this actor performs); `:order-supplies` above a 5000 USD cost\n   threshold (`governor/supply-order-cost-threshold-usd`) likewise\n   always escalates, while at or below the threshold it may auto-commit\n   when the Governor is otherwise clean.\n5. **`forestrysupport.phase`** -- `:intake -> :survey -> :advise ->\n   :treat -> :record -> :audit`. This sequence was NOT invented fresh: it\n   is the registry's own already-registered `:operating-states` for\n   `\"0240\"` (present since the entry's original `:spec` placeholder, and\n   identical to `\"0161\"`'s own sequence), confirmed meaningful (not a\n   placeholder sequence) and adopted verbatim rather than overwritten.\n   Uses the same portable `keep-indexed`-based `index-of` helper 0161\n   established (not the JVM-only `.indexOf`), so this actor ships\n   cljs-portable from day one.\n6. **`deps.edn` / `blueprint.edn` / docs** -- mirror\n   `cloud-itonami-isic-0161`'s shape (`:test`/`:lint`/`:run`/`:dev`\n   aliases, `itonami.blueprint/*` metadata, scope/design/testing README\n   sections). `:itonami.blueprint/robotics` is honestly `false` (this\n   actor holds no chainsaw/skidder/patrol-vehicle-control authority).\n\n### What this actor does NOT do\n\nOperating a chainsaw, skidder, or patrol vehicle remains exclusive to the\nlicensed field-equipment operator in the field, permanently, with no actor\nor human-approval override path -- enforced structurally by both the\nclosed operation allowlist and the dedicated\n`forestry-equipment-or-fire-tactic-decision-blocked` defense-in-depth\ncheck, not just documented. This actor also does not finalize a\nfire-suppression-tactic decision on its own (same permanent block), and\ndoes not fell or otherwise harvest timber -- that is ISIC's\ntimber-harvesting divisions (022x), out of scope entirely.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-0240`: `clojure -M:test` -- raw final line: `Ran 48\n  tests containing 181 assertions.` / `0 failures, 0 errors.` (re-run\n  green a second time from a brand-new fresh clone after push).\n- `clojure -M:lint` -- 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- All source under `src/`/`test/` is `.cljc`; the only host-clock call\n  (`now-epoch-ms` in `forestrysupport.governor`) is behind a `:clj`/\n  `:cljs` reader conditional, no stray JVM-only interop.\n- Repo created fresh (`gh repo create` + push), initial commit\n  `c34cd289d633041ca13c695ebea78d44c8e5767b` on\n  `cloud-itonami-isic-0240`'s `main` (no prior history), confirmed via\n  `git rev-parse HEAD` == the branch tip returned by the GitHub commits\n  API.\n- `kotoba-lang/industry` registry `\"0240\"` entry updated in place (exact-\n  text edit of the literal `{:id \"0240\" ...}` block only, no other\n  entry's block touched -- verified programmatically by reconstructing\n  the pre-edit file from the post-edit file and diffing byte-for-byte):\n  `:repo`/`:business-id` corrected from the never-populated\n  `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0240` placeholder to\n  `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0240` / `cloud-itonami-isic-0240`,\n  `:maturity` `:spec` -> `:implemented`, `:required-technologies`/\n  `:optional-technologies`/`:operating-states` left as already\n  registered. Landed via a Contents API single-file PUT (sha-checked\n  optimistic concurrency), commit `64f22651e8f67f792bc1ccd458df986c862bf2a5`.\n- `test/kotoba/industry_test.clj`'s `maturity-summary` assertion bumped\n  (live-recomputed via `(industry/maturity-summary)` against a freshly\n  re-fetched `origin/main` immediately before each edit, not assumed --\n  this is an extremely hot, high-concurrency shared file). Landed in\n  three Contents API PUTs as the live count kept advancing from\n  concurrent sibling promotions during this work: the promotion block\n  itself plus an initial `359 -> 360` bump (commit\n  `c0ec6b536de62b9a21c4471f2d16501c5d2de640`), a same-day ADR-number\n  self-correction inside the just-added testing-block narration text\n  (this ADR's own timestamp moved from an initial `2611300000` pick to\n  `2613100000` after the live ADR directory advanced past it during this\n  work -- commit `938e0fc8acde812b50380bbba142aa469bfa21e2`), and a final\n  live-recompute `360 -> 364` (two further concurrent sibling promotions\n  had landed by then -- commit\n  `20f4bab8f0874c5c03b777f65c3dc8b003b7d700`). Each PUT re-fetched the\n  file's current sha and content immediately before building the edit\n  (never reused an older buffer), per this fleet's hot-contention\n  discipline.\n- Full `kotoba-lang/industry` suite re-run green after all edits (fresh\n  clone, plus a fresh `kotoba-lang/technology` sibling clone for\n  `deps.edn` resolution): `Ran 15 tests containing 1025 assertions.` /\n  `0 failures, 0 errors.` `kotoba-lang/industry` main tip after all PUTs:\n  `e727dc6e8ed14fcea50ec4fcde65744a67e4631f`.\n- Final post-merge re-verification (brand-new scratch directory, fresh\n  `origin/main` clone of both `cloud-itonami-isic-0240` and\n  `kotoba-lang/industry`, plus a fresh `kotoba-lang/technology` sibling):\n  `clojure -M:test` re-run green in both repos; the registry's `\"0240\"`\n  entry confirmed `:maturity :implemented` with the corrected\n  `:repo`/`:business-id`, and sibling entries `\"0161\"`/`\"0170\"` confirmed\n  untouched. `(industry/maturity-summary)` on the final tip returned\n  `{:total 648, :spec 259, :blueprint 25, :implemented 364}`, matching\n  the test file's bumped assertion. `grep -c` for the UTF-8 replacement\n  character against `resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` returned\n  `0` (no file-wide mojibake).\n\n## Consequences\n\n(+) `cloud-itonami-isic-0240` now has a real, tested implementation\nmatching the shape of every other cloud-itonami ISIC actor, replacing a\nplaceholder registry entry that pointed at a repo that never existed.\n(+) `kotoba-lang/industry` registry `\"0240\"` entry promoted to `:maturity\n:implemented`.\n(+) `forestrysupport.facts`/`forestrysupport.governor`'s asymmetric\nper-service-type `nil`-guarded physical-constraint checks (not every\nfield-equipment-operation service type carries every one of\nwind-speed/riparian-buffer/load-limit) extend the pattern\n`cloud-itonami-isic-0170` established for trap-vs-direct-take harvest\nmethods to a third distinct shape: within a single \"field-equipment-\noperation\" category, individual physical-constraint fields can still be\ngenuinely inapplicable to a specific service type, not just to an entire\ncategory -- a reusable pattern for any future ISIC class in this fleet's\nagriculture/forestry/fishing cluster with this finer-grained shape.\n(+) The per-service-type equipment-inspection interval (30 days for\nfire-protection-support vs. 60 days for log-haul, rather than a single\nhardcoded window) demonstrates a genuine domain difference the tests\ncaught during development, distinct from 0161's single fixed 90-day\nsprayer-calibration window.\n(-) `forestrysupport.advisor` remains a documentation-only stub (no\n`MockAdvisor` implementation); `forestrysupport.operation/run-operation`\ntakes an already-formed proposal plus an injected `governor-fn` rather\nthan internally invoking an advisor. This matches\n`cloud-itonami-isic-0161`'s own current shape and is a natural, contained\nfuture extension, not required for this ADR's verification bar.\n"), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/date "2026-07-16"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2613100000: cloud-itonami-isic-0240 (Support services to forestry) forestry-support-service operations-coordination actor -- fresh scaffold, full implementation"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))